{% comment %}
  Product page presentation fixes.

  Mobile above-the-fold. Measured on the Purple Bearbrick page at 375x812
  before the fix: .tdp-thumbs wrapped 12 thumbnails onto 3 rows (178px),
  gallery total 528px, price at y=874 - below the fold. Collapsing the strip
  to one scrollable row and capping the hero image reclaims ~165px and lifts
  the price to y=708, about 104px above the fold.

  Note on the specs panel: .tdp-hspec ships collapsed and stays that way by
  design. An open-by-default version was tried and reverted - opening it adds
  ~155px between the price and the buy button, which pushed Add to cart 176px
  below the fold on desktop. If specs visibility is revisited, the better fix
  is moving the panel below the buy button in diorama-product.liquid rather
  than expanding it in place.

  These overrides belong in sections/diorama-product.liquid alongside the rest
  of the product CSS; they live here only to avoid rewriting that 74KB file
  wholesale. Fold them in next time that file is edited.
{% endcomment %}

{%- if template.name == 'product' and product != blank -%}
  <style>
    @media (max-width: 749px) {
      .tdp-gallery .tdp-thumbs {
        flex-wrap: nowrap;
        overflow-x: auto;
        overflow-y: hidden;
        scrollbar-width: none;
        -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
      }
      .tdp-gallery .tdp-thumbs::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
      .tdp-gallery .tdp-thumb { flex: 0 0 auto; }

      .tdp-gallery .tdp-main-img { max-height: 300px; }
      .tdp-gallery .tdp-main-img img {
        max-height: 300px;
        object-fit: contain;
      }
    }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "PDP presentation fixes",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
